{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Concept of Information Management"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to discuss the importance of information management."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Learning Outcome"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Participates in simple conversations or simulated situations about the communicative topics for this level through grammar and vocabulary structures.  Recognizes simple ideas on requirement reports, tools for Object Oriented Programming, and other basic programming tools."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Verbs with Infinitives and Infinitives of Purpose"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "In English, there are some verbs that are followed with <span class=\"strong\">infinitives</span>  when we want to use them with other verbs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Infinitives of purpose</span> are verbs that follow the preposition <span class=\"strong\">to</span> in order to express the purpose or intention of the action.<br /><br />  Examples:<br /> <span class=\"italic\">It is important to manage information in an organized way <span class=\"strong\">to coordinate</span> processes effectively.<br /> I collect requirements <span class=\"strong\">to sort</span> them later.</span><br /><br />  In the first example, we can see that the <span class=\"strong\">reason</span> or <span class=\"strong\">intention</span> to manage information is <span class=\"strong\">to coordinate</span> processes effectively.<br /><br />  Let's discuss verbs with infinitives. <br /><br />  <span class=\"strong\">Verbs with infinitives</span> are verbs that need the preposition <span class=\"strong\">to</span> in order to introduce another verb. The second verb is in the infinitive form, while the first verb can be in any tense you need it.<br /><br />  Examples:<br /> <span class=\"italic\">We don't <span class=\"strong\">need to implement</span> a new software.<br /> They <span class=\"strong\">planning to design</span> a new system.<br /> I <span class=\"strong\">have to sort</span> out the requirements.</span><br /><br />  Not all verbs can be accompanied by <span class=\"strong\">infinitives</span>. In the chart below, you can find some of the most common verbs followed by <span class=\"strong\">infinitives</span>. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verbs with Infinitives\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Need to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We <span class=\\\"strong\\\">need to work</span> on the system.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Have to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have to collect </span> all the requirements.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Want to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">She <span class=\\\"strong\\\">wants to implement </span> new software.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Plan to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We're <span class=\\\"strong\\\">planning to change  </span> the software design.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Last night, I went online to research on information management."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If they want to implement new services to grow their brand, information management helps stakeholders handle and control inside information by deploying new technology."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I decided to read up on that."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Idioms on Information"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Idioms</span> are expressions people use to make speech more natural and informal. Each of the words in an idiom usually has a meaning that is different when you use it alone."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Idioms</span> are expressions which cannot be predicted from the literal meaning of the words because they have a contextual significance. <br /><br /> There are many idioms related to technology. In the chart below, you can find some idioms related to communication and information."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Idioms with information\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Nugget of information\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Used when someone tells you something very interesting you didn't know \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"To worm information\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"To find out information from someone who is reluctant to talk about the subject \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"For your information\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"An expression you use to introduce a piece of information\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Gold mine of information\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Referring to someone or something that knows a lot about any topic \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Inside information\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Secret information that only a selected group of people know\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Too much information\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Used when someone tells you something private or embarrassing\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "custodianship "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the condition of having the custody of something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is also a set of organizational activities that involve the acquisition, custodianship, distribution, and ultimate disposition of information."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "deploy "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to dispose, to arrange "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If they want to implement new services to grow their brand, information management helps stakeholders handle and control inside information by deploying new technology."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "overlap "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to coincide with something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Information management overlaps with data management systems and technology."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "employ"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to use, to apply "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Companies employ content management systems, data warehousing, or portal applications for storage and disposal."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob05aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "read up on "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to learn about  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I decided to read up on that, and I found out that, in 1970s, information management concerned things that now we call data management."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob05aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for more information about information management in the 1970's, 1980's and 1990's."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a comparison chart in a poster."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Describe the main differences between management of information in those decades and the present by showing their importance for the enterprises."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your final product with your classmates and instructor. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find and read information about information management."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a comparison chart by showing the evolution and importance for enterprises."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I show and explain my work to my classmates and instructor. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n3le01ob05re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n3le01ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Louise:</span> Hey, Bob! I saw you online very late last night. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Bob:</span> Hi, Louise! Yes. Last night, I went online to research on information management.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Louise:</span> Oh, I see. I guess that's the assignment for The Basics of Programming II, right? What did you find out? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Bob:</span> Actually, I learned a lot. Information management is a key concept in requirement analysis. It is also a set of organizational activities that involve the acquisition, custodianship, distribution, and ultimate disposition of information. When we talk about information management, it also includes important actions such as organizing, planning, processing, structuring, evaluating, controlling, and reporting to meet the needs of functions that are the base of information.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Louise:</span>  Wow! That's a nugget of information. When did it all begin?"}, {"time": "56000", "image": "enpe8n3le01ob05re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Bob:</span> I decided to read up on that, and I found out that, in the 1970s, information management concerned things that now we call data management. They actually used magnetic tapes and punched cards! In the 80s and 90s, information management took a new form. Nowadays, it is essential for companies to focus on that. If they want to improve the efficiency of business processes to offer a better service, or if they want to implement new services to grow their brand, information management helps stakeholders handle and control inside information by deploying new technology. It's an essential issue."}, {"time": "97000", "image": "enpe8n3le01ob05re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Louise:</span> What kind of new technology? Can you give me some examples?   <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Bob:</span> Sure! Companies need to use the information management cycle to collect and communicate information within organizations. For example, companies employ content management systems, data warehousing, or portal applications for storage and disposal, making it easier for stakeholders, and those who need it, to access information for decision making. Information management overlaps with data management systems and technology.   <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Louise:</span> Now I understand why you were online until late, you had to study a lot! Definitely, the internet is a gold mine of information. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Bob:</span> That's right, Louise, information management is a very complex but necessary process for companies."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n3le01ob05re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain the concept of information management."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can give examples related to information management."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can identify the importance of information management for an enterprise."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Why do you think companies care for information management?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What software do you know to manage information? What are its characteristics?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner: "}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "The importance of information management"}], "id": 0,